1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,855
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:08,000
Come on.

3
00:00:13,625 --> 00:00:14,458
Come on.

4
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:21,416
Hang in there. Wan will be here soon.

5
00:00:25,416 --> 00:00:26,500
Swamp Eel.

6
00:00:27,583 --> 00:00:29,000
If I die,

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,125
please take care of Chia-yun and her mom.

8
00:00:34,125 --> 00:00:35,500
Take care, my ass.

9
00:00:35,583 --> 00:00:38,458
Take care of them yourself. Do you understand?

10
00:00:40,375 --> 00:00:41,708
Fuck, who am I?

11
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:44,041
Swamp Eel. I rise to power by shooting flies.

12
00:00:44,958 --> 00:00:47,041
You will be fine with me here.

13
00:00:47,541 --> 00:00:48,375
Don't worry.

14
00:00:50,416 --> 00:00:51,958
Hang in there. It'll be fine.

15
00:00:52,041 --> 00:00:53,541
Hang in there, you hear me?

16
00:00:54,541 --> 00:00:55,666
Stop! Over there!

17
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:56,750
-Fuck. -Go down here.

18
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,208
They're coming.

19
00:00:58,708 --> 00:01:02,500
Swamp Eel, go. Wan and the others aren't coming.

20
00:01:03,208 --> 00:01:05,250
Don't worry, they will come.

21
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:06,333
They will come.

22
00:01:07,166 --> 00:01:09,416
You're lying to yourself.

23
00:01:09,916 --> 00:01:11,291
If they were coming,

24
00:01:11,375 --> 00:01:13,583
they would be here already.

25
00:01:14,791 --> 00:01:15,708
Got it?

26
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:24,625
Hang in there.

27
00:01:26,125 --> 00:01:26,958
Don't worry.

28
00:01:27,458 --> 00:01:29,625
You will be fine with me here.

29
00:01:37,416 --> 00:01:38,958
Hang in there. It'll be fine.

30
00:01:39,041 --> 00:01:40,333
Hang in there, you hear me?

31
00:01:40,416 --> 00:01:41,416
Fucking hang in there!

32
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:42,416
Hang in there.

33
00:02:14,166 --> 00:02:15,666
I finally have the chance…

34
00:02:22,208 --> 00:02:24,541
to take the shot I didn't get to take before.

35
00:02:32,458 --> 00:02:34,458
You still think about Chi?

36
00:02:34,541 --> 00:02:36,208
As long as I'm still alive,

37
00:02:36,708 --> 00:02:38,291
I will never let it go.

38
00:02:39,875 --> 00:02:40,708
Lin Wan-li,

39
00:02:41,708 --> 00:02:43,166
you weren't fit to be our boss.

40
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:49,375
Anyway, once I leave the mountain,

41
00:02:49,458 --> 00:02:52,291
I will die at my own brother's hands.

42
00:02:53,916 --> 00:02:55,875
I would rather die at yours.

43
00:02:58,708 --> 00:03:00,041
Go on and shoot.

44
00:03:00,541 --> 00:03:01,500
Bastard.

45
00:03:01,583 --> 00:03:03,708
You told us to ambush those traitors.

46
00:03:03,791 --> 00:03:06,458
You said you'd send more men. But then what?

47
00:03:07,416 --> 00:03:09,958
Chi's death was all your fault!

48
00:03:11,125 --> 00:03:13,166
They were prepared

49
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:14,833
and had powerful backers.

50
00:03:14,916 --> 00:03:16,625
If I had sent men to rescue you,

51
00:03:17,125 --> 00:03:19,583
it would have only led to more deaths.

52
00:03:21,166 --> 00:03:22,875
If I could do it all over again,

53
00:03:24,166 --> 00:03:26,333
I would still make the same decision.

54
00:03:33,583 --> 00:03:34,416
Swamp Eel,

55
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:38,916
tell Wan that I'm going on ahead.

56
00:03:40,458 --> 00:03:42,125
Tell him to take care.

57
00:04:09,291 --> 00:04:10,458
Do you know?

58
00:04:12,375 --> 00:04:13,916
Up until Chi died…

59
00:04:16,458 --> 00:04:18,208
he still called you "boss."

60
00:04:21,083 --> 00:04:22,166
Remember.

61
00:04:22,833 --> 00:04:24,166
You owe your life

62
00:04:24,916 --> 00:04:26,083
to him.

63
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:57,166
You are awake, so you'll be fine.

64
00:05:28,833 --> 00:05:31,000
THE FIXERS

65
00:05:32,291 --> 00:05:35,666
ONE SHORT

66
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:38,125
Sweetie, don't worry.

67
00:05:38,208 --> 00:05:40,125
It's just my ear that got a little injured.

68
00:05:40,625 --> 00:05:41,750
I'm fine.

69
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:45,333
Pin and Hsiu, those two idiots.

70
00:05:45,416 --> 00:05:47,625
They've nearly split up San He.

71
00:05:47,708 --> 00:05:49,958
After I take care of things, I'll come home.

72
00:05:50,875 --> 00:05:52,708
Okay, that's all for now.

73
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:57,083
Hsiu, our men saw with their own eyes

74
00:05:57,166 --> 00:05:59,125
that your men kidnapped my brother.

75
00:05:59,208 --> 00:06:01,375
You got the ransom.

76
00:06:02,083 --> 00:06:03,875
If anything happens to my brother,

77
00:06:03,958 --> 00:06:05,041
I will make you pay.

78
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:06,416
It could have also been you.

79
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,500
What did you say?

80
00:06:13,208 --> 00:06:14,416
Enough!

81
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:21,708
What's going on? Why are you all crowding? Step back!

82
00:06:21,791 --> 00:06:24,708
Boss.

83
00:06:26,583 --> 00:06:28,083
Is this a stare-down?

84
00:06:28,583 --> 00:06:29,583
Back off!

85
00:06:33,166 --> 00:06:34,375
Pin,

86
00:06:34,458 --> 00:06:38,333
my brother, thank goodness that you sent men to look for me.

87
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:39,875
However,

88
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,125
the two guys who kidnapped me

89
00:06:42,208 --> 00:06:44,416
had nothing to do with Hsiu.

90
00:06:45,125 --> 00:06:46,916
What did I say before?

91
00:06:47,791 --> 00:06:49,875
Harmony above all.

92
00:06:51,541 --> 00:06:54,666
It was all a misunderstanding.

93
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:56,208
For my sake,

94
00:06:56,708 --> 00:06:58,791
let it be.

95
00:06:59,958 --> 00:07:03,583
We must look after each other at San He,

96
00:07:03,666 --> 00:07:05,666
so outsiders can't take advantage of us.

97
00:07:06,666 --> 00:07:08,166
Since everyone is here,

98
00:07:08,666 --> 00:07:10,333
I'll take this opportunity

99
00:07:10,833 --> 00:07:12,416
to make an announcement.

100
00:07:20,708 --> 00:07:22,500
This younger brother of mine

101
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:27,750
has coveted my seat for a long time.

102
00:07:29,291 --> 00:07:32,666
I've let down too many people who called me their boss over the years.

103
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,625
It's time to step down.

104
00:07:38,083 --> 00:07:38,916
Are you sure

105
00:07:39,833 --> 00:07:42,083
you want to hand the seat over to your brother?

106
00:07:43,833 --> 00:07:47,500
Starting today, everything related to San He

107
00:07:47,583 --> 00:07:51,250
will be handled by my brother, Lin Kuei-pin.

108
00:07:51,833 --> 00:07:53,208
I am retiring.

109
00:07:59,583 --> 00:08:02,833
You have to be ruthless when you make your move.

110
00:08:02,916 --> 00:08:06,375
Show no mercy, even to your own family, when necessary.

111
00:08:07,458 --> 00:08:09,125
Like this time,

112
00:08:10,083 --> 00:08:13,708
you wanted to take me, your own brother, out.

113
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:15,666
In this regard,

114
00:08:16,166 --> 00:08:17,833
you do a better job than I do.

115
00:08:19,541 --> 00:08:20,916
San He

116
00:08:21,916 --> 00:08:23,208
is in your hands now.

117
00:08:30,416 --> 00:08:33,875
Hsiu has helped us handle the situation with Fixer Shadow.

118
00:08:34,375 --> 00:08:36,291
For people like us,

119
00:08:36,375 --> 00:08:39,166
taking the blame for others is no big deal.

120
00:08:42,791 --> 00:08:45,000
You are a major client of Ching He.

121
00:08:45,583 --> 00:08:48,166
If you spread the word,

122
00:08:48,666 --> 00:08:50,958
people will believe it.

123
00:08:51,041 --> 00:08:54,000
Who on earth dares target Ching He's men?

124
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,166
Hey, eat more swamp eel.

125
00:09:03,250 --> 00:09:06,041
It helps replenish blood and build muscle. Good for recovery.

126
00:09:07,625 --> 00:09:09,791
Holy shit.

127
00:09:09,875 --> 00:09:12,000
Truth is stranger than fiction.

128
00:09:12,083 --> 00:09:14,041
This is practically a mansion.

129
00:09:14,541 --> 00:09:15,750
-Lucky. -Yeah?

130
00:09:15,833 --> 00:09:17,833
Sit. Greet our guest.

131
00:09:21,083 --> 00:09:23,208
Goddamn, is it also called Lucky?

132
00:09:23,291 --> 00:09:24,250
Is that on purpose?

133
00:09:24,958 --> 00:09:26,041
What do you think?

134
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:28,208
How are you?

135
00:09:28,291 --> 00:09:29,500
Is the wound any better?

136
00:09:29,583 --> 00:09:30,583
It won't kill me.

137
00:09:31,083 --> 00:09:33,833
Let me tell you, you got real lucky you had me.

138
00:09:33,916 --> 00:09:37,083
If anyone else had treated that wound, you would've been done for.

139
00:09:37,166 --> 00:09:39,750
When I was young, I was shot three times.

140
00:09:39,833 --> 00:09:42,041
Left shoulder, right abdomen, and left thigh.

141
00:09:42,125 --> 00:09:44,500
Two words sum it up. Close call.

142
00:09:47,750 --> 00:09:49,750
Aren't you gonna ask what happened next?

143
00:09:49,833 --> 00:09:50,833
Aren't you alive now?

144
00:09:51,708 --> 00:09:52,583
Why ask?

145
00:09:55,583 --> 00:09:59,000
You're like a brick wall. I might as well talk to my buddy, Lucky.

146
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:00,750
Lucky, come here.

147
00:10:01,416 --> 00:10:03,041
Holy cow.

148
00:10:06,458 --> 00:10:10,791
He looks so familiar. Isn't he running for mayor?

149
00:10:10,875 --> 00:10:12,500
He's been on the news a lot lately.

150
00:10:12,583 --> 00:10:15,041
-Why are you in a photo together? -Why so many questions?

151
00:10:15,125 --> 00:10:16,166
Wait.

152
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:18,416
You two look alike.

153
00:10:19,750 --> 00:10:20,958
He's my older brother.

154
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:23,625
He's your older brother?

155
00:10:24,208 --> 00:10:25,375
Holy shit.

156
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:28,333
Hey, why would someone like you work as a fixer?

157
00:10:28,416 --> 00:10:29,666
Are you out of your mind?

158
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:32,375
Can't I do what makes me happy? Eat your noodles.

159
00:10:33,958 --> 00:10:35,166
Got it.

160
00:10:35,666 --> 00:10:37,708
Everyone has their own secrets.

161
00:10:38,291 --> 00:10:40,541
But you look more like the older brother.

162
00:10:41,916 --> 00:10:43,125
Why don't you tell me

163
00:10:43,625 --> 00:10:45,500
why you spared Lin Wan-li that day?

164
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:59,458
BELOVED FATHER, CHEN LIANG-CHI

165
00:11:05,875 --> 00:11:07,500
BELOVED MOTHER, WANG SHU-HUA

166
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:09,750
Dad. Mom.

167
00:11:10,958 --> 00:11:12,791
I got into a US college.

168
00:11:14,416 --> 00:11:17,291
I might not be able to visit as often in the future.

169
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,708
Chi, exceptional children come from humble origins too.

170
00:11:28,250 --> 00:11:32,041
Look how amazing Chen Chia-yun is. She's going to study in the US.

171
00:11:34,458 --> 00:11:37,250
Don't be sad that she is leaving.

172
00:11:37,333 --> 00:11:40,500
Watch over her and make sure everything goes smoothly.

173
00:11:40,583 --> 00:11:43,125
Better yet, she brings home a boyfriend from abroad.

174
00:11:47,916 --> 00:11:48,750
Come on.

175
00:12:00,625 --> 00:12:02,250
Mom, I'm doing great.

176
00:12:04,125 --> 00:12:06,416
Tristan looks after me. Don't worry.

177
00:12:07,541 --> 00:12:09,625
We still play tennis together often,

178
00:12:09,708 --> 00:12:11,291
although he can't beat me.

179
00:12:17,375 --> 00:12:18,291
Dad…

180
00:12:18,791 --> 00:12:21,625
Dad has been rather busy lately.

181
00:12:22,625 --> 00:12:25,333
So he can't visit you. Don't take it to heart.

182
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:32,000
If only you were still here.

183
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:45,458
DAD

184
00:13:02,083 --> 00:13:04,166
From my great-grandfather, a legislator,

185
00:13:04,833 --> 00:13:06,333
to my father,

186
00:13:06,416 --> 00:13:09,583
they have dedicated their lives to serving the people.

187
00:13:09,666 --> 00:13:11,625
It's now my turn to take up the baton.

188
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:15,083
I will carry their legacy forward and continue to serve the people.

189
00:13:15,583 --> 00:13:18,250
I would like to give special thanks to my mother today.

190
00:13:19,041 --> 00:13:21,958
She has always been the quiet strength of our family.

191
00:13:22,541 --> 00:13:25,583
Without her, we wouldn't be where we are today.

192
00:13:51,791 --> 00:13:53,333
So today is a date?

193
00:13:58,583 --> 00:13:59,625
I need a favor.

194
00:14:02,583 --> 00:14:03,416
Why should I help?

195
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:04,541
I saved your life.

196
00:14:07,083 --> 00:14:08,333
I looked for Lin Wan-li

197
00:14:09,083 --> 00:14:10,375
to ask about someone.

198
00:14:11,666 --> 00:14:13,291
Is it related to that necklace?

199
00:14:13,375 --> 00:14:14,208
Yes.

200
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,208
Why are you looking for them?

201
00:14:17,875 --> 00:14:19,583
He is very important to me.

202
00:14:22,125 --> 00:14:23,500
His name is Gerald Chen.

203
00:14:23,583 --> 00:14:26,625
He used to be a fixer for Yeh Yueh Tong.

204
00:14:28,458 --> 00:14:31,208
Over a year ago, he suddenly vanished.

205
00:14:32,125 --> 00:14:33,750
Lin Wan-li said Gerald went to him.

206
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:38,000
Gerald did come to see me.

207
00:14:38,958 --> 00:14:41,583
It was about Yuan Tao Group's founder,

208
00:14:41,666 --> 00:14:42,875
Zoe.

209
00:14:42,958 --> 00:14:44,750
But I refused him.

210
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:47,333
I didn't want anything to do with Yeh Yueh Tong.

211
00:14:47,416 --> 00:14:48,416
We believe that…

212
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:51,583
Zoe, one of Yuan Tao's founders.

213
00:14:51,666 --> 00:14:52,958
Our future goals are…

214
00:14:53,041 --> 00:14:55,791
Over a year ago, she died in an accident in Vietnam.

215
00:14:55,875 --> 00:14:58,458
Around the same time Gerald went missing.

216
00:14:58,541 --> 00:15:00,333
If I can get into Yuan Tao,

217
00:15:00,833 --> 00:15:02,291
maybe I can find him.

218
00:15:04,708 --> 00:15:07,875
I just met with Zoe's sister here.

219
00:15:09,125 --> 00:15:10,500
You posed as Zoe's friend?

220
00:15:10,583 --> 00:15:12,416
A college classmate when she was abroad.

221
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:15,708
I came back hoping to catch up with her.

222
00:15:16,208 --> 00:15:18,166
I had no idea she passed away.

223
00:15:18,791 --> 00:15:21,416
What about her partner? Is he doing okay?

224
00:15:22,125 --> 00:15:23,833
Her husband is gone.

225
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:26,916
My sister had a happy family.

226
00:15:27,916 --> 00:15:29,291
I never expected…

227
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:33,000
Zoe's husband was a legislative aide.

228
00:15:33,666 --> 00:15:35,458
Not long before her accident,

229
00:15:35,541 --> 00:15:36,666
he committed suicide.

230
00:15:37,416 --> 00:15:38,791
Does her sister know about Gerald?

231
00:15:40,666 --> 00:15:43,583
But she did mention Yuan Tao's other founder,

232
00:15:43,666 --> 00:15:44,666
William.

233
00:15:44,750 --> 00:15:46,875
We believe the value of blockchain technology…

234
00:15:46,958 --> 00:15:49,958
My sister and William had a falling out.

235
00:15:50,458 --> 00:15:52,875
I don't want to go around suspecting people, but

236
00:15:52,958 --> 00:15:55,500
I heard them fighting over the phone.

237
00:15:55,583 --> 00:15:59,916
Zoe said William destroyed her years of hard work building the company.

238
00:16:00,416 --> 00:16:03,000
So you suspect that he is connected to Zoe's death.

239
00:16:03,083 --> 00:16:04,958
He must know about Zoe.

240
00:16:05,041 --> 00:16:09,125
He might lead us to more clues about Gerald.

241
00:16:10,416 --> 00:16:11,833
I need your help.

242
00:16:14,875 --> 00:16:17,083
Why don't you ask Yeh Yueh Tong?

243
00:16:18,958 --> 00:16:21,458
As the second son of the Hsueh family,

244
00:16:22,291 --> 00:16:24,666
you should have an easier time

245
00:16:24,750 --> 00:16:26,291
approaching the cofounder.

246
00:16:28,791 --> 00:16:30,125
When did you find out?

247
00:16:31,125 --> 00:16:33,000
Did you think you hid it well?

248
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:40,458
Lately, besides Fixer Lucky,

249
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:43,000
you seem to have made a new friend from Yeh Yueh Tong.

250
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:44,958
We're not close.

251
00:16:45,458 --> 00:16:48,750
But she did help with Lin Wan-li's case.

252
00:16:49,666 --> 00:16:51,708
I don't mean to pursue it.

253
00:16:51,791 --> 00:16:55,041
Otherwise, I wouldn't have waited until now.

254
00:16:55,541 --> 00:16:57,083
Did you get the necklace back?

255
00:16:58,208 --> 00:16:59,375
I did.

256
00:17:01,208 --> 00:17:06,208
I heard you have been close with a fixer from Ching He.

257
00:17:06,708 --> 00:17:08,791
I was just getting my stuff back.

258
00:17:11,791 --> 00:17:14,875
I didn't tell her anything about Ching He.

259
00:17:17,375 --> 00:17:21,041
It isn't a bad thing to have a friend from Yeh Yueh Tong.

260
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:24,625
Of all the fixers, I trust you the most.

261
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,791
There are some things you should know.

262
00:17:30,291 --> 00:17:31,750
Back then, Fixer Lunar,

263
00:17:31,833 --> 00:17:34,708
who is now Madam Fan of Yeh Yueh Tong,

264
00:17:35,208 --> 00:17:37,083
and her father

265
00:17:37,166 --> 00:17:39,291
broke Ching He's rules.

266
00:17:39,791 --> 00:17:41,583
That's why all the branches

267
00:17:41,666 --> 00:17:44,125
elected me as Fixer Celestial.

268
00:17:44,958 --> 00:17:49,041
Of course, Madam Fan has been holding a grudge over this.

269
00:17:49,625 --> 00:17:50,875
A word of warning.

270
00:17:51,458 --> 00:17:54,291
Soon, it won't be peaceful at Ching He.

271
00:17:54,375 --> 00:17:55,541
So I'm worried

272
00:17:56,041 --> 00:17:59,416
that there's a lot of trouble coming.

273
00:18:00,375 --> 00:18:01,791
Be more careful.

274
00:18:01,875 --> 00:18:03,708
Don't get dragged into it.

275
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:07,208
If Yeh Yueh Tong does anything that harms Ching He,

276
00:18:07,291 --> 00:18:08,166
I will tell you.

277
00:18:10,791 --> 00:18:14,750
Yeh Yueh Tong wasn't hired by San He this time.

278
00:18:14,833 --> 00:18:17,166
How did Madam Fan find out?

279
00:18:17,666 --> 00:18:19,041
Yeh Yueh Tong wasn't involved.

280
00:18:19,541 --> 00:18:21,875
Mina Shen wanted to ask Lin Wan-li about someone.

281
00:18:23,625 --> 00:18:24,708
Who?

282
00:18:24,791 --> 00:18:27,166
Gerald Chen, also from Yeh Yueh Tong.

283
00:18:29,250 --> 00:18:32,958
Every time I see you, I think of Gerald.

284
00:18:33,708 --> 00:18:35,583
If he hadn't gone missing,

285
00:18:36,083 --> 00:18:40,958
you two would have been Yeh Yueh Tong's best fixers.

286
00:18:42,125 --> 00:18:43,875
I want to find him more than you do.

287
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:48,958
Are you sure that it's Mina who wants to find Gerald

288
00:18:49,708 --> 00:18:52,125
and not Yeh Yueh Tong?

289
00:18:52,791 --> 00:18:53,875
I'm certain.

290
00:18:55,958 --> 00:18:56,958
Madam Fan,

291
00:18:57,666 --> 00:19:00,291
were we ever hired by Yuan Tao?

292
00:19:00,791 --> 00:19:04,291
Yuan Tao never hired Yeh Yueh Tong.

293
00:19:06,208 --> 00:19:07,791
Anything else?

294
00:19:07,875 --> 00:19:08,708
No.

295
00:19:17,958 --> 00:19:20,333
CHRONIC GI DISCOMFORT? BEWARE OF PARKINSON'S!

296
00:19:22,333 --> 00:19:24,791
WESTERN MEDICINE: PARKINSON'S MAY START IN THE GUT

297
00:19:34,208 --> 00:19:35,916
GOLDIE

298
00:19:38,041 --> 00:19:40,000
When did you get another cell phone?

299
00:19:40,750 --> 00:19:41,875
Who is this Goldie?

300
00:19:41,958 --> 00:19:42,916
A customer.

301
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:43,875
A man or a woman?

302
00:19:43,958 --> 00:19:45,583
A man.

303
00:19:46,375 --> 00:19:48,333
Do you actually have a mistress?

304
00:19:48,416 --> 00:19:49,458
What mistress?

305
00:19:49,541 --> 00:19:50,875
This is a work cell phone.

306
00:19:50,958 --> 00:19:52,458
Then who is this Goldie?

307
00:19:52,541 --> 00:19:54,166
I'll tell you who she is later.

308
00:19:54,250 --> 00:19:56,291
No, I mean, Goldie.

309
00:19:56,375 --> 00:19:58,583
You're the one bringing up a mistress.

310
00:19:58,666 --> 00:20:00,625
I won't let this go until you explain!

311
00:20:01,208 --> 00:20:03,500
Felix, I'm not done talking!

312
00:20:06,250 --> 00:20:09,416
STIR-FRIED SWAMP EEL, SWAMP EEL NOODLES

313
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:10,750
Can I ask you something?

314
00:20:12,583 --> 00:20:13,666
You go first.

315
00:20:14,333 --> 00:20:15,583
Okay, I…

316
00:20:15,666 --> 00:20:19,583
Have you heard of something called "Parinsane's disease"?

317
00:20:20,333 --> 00:20:21,291
Parkinson's.

318
00:20:21,375 --> 00:20:23,208
-Yes, "Parsonkin's." -"Parkin."

319
00:20:24,125 --> 00:20:25,958
Gosh. Anyway…

320
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:30,375
Anyway, the doctor… The doctor says I have that disease.

321
00:20:35,625 --> 00:20:38,833
What's the matter with you? How come you don't respond to others?

322
00:20:38,916 --> 00:20:40,708
And you're such a picky eater.

323
00:20:40,791 --> 00:20:43,375
Just listen to the doctor and don't overthink it.

324
00:20:45,416 --> 00:20:47,125
Aren't you afraid I'll burden you?

325
00:20:47,875 --> 00:20:50,083
I noticed your hand tremors a while ago.

326
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:52,708
I know some top doctors who treat wealthy patients.

327
00:20:52,791 --> 00:20:54,250
I'll introduce them to you.

328
00:20:55,958 --> 00:20:58,000
I was wondering

329
00:20:58,083 --> 00:21:00,625
if you want to find a new partner.

330
00:21:00,708 --> 00:21:01,958
I can't.

331
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:04,166
No one else wants to be my partner.

332
00:21:06,208 --> 00:21:08,000
Your turn. What were you going to ask?

333
00:21:08,083 --> 00:21:09,083
Mina.

334
00:21:09,583 --> 00:21:11,875
She's using Lin Wan-li's leads to look for someone.

335
00:21:11,958 --> 00:21:12,791
I want you in.

336
00:21:12,875 --> 00:21:13,833
Okay, no problem.

337
00:21:13,916 --> 00:21:15,500
I haven't even said who it is.

338
00:21:15,583 --> 00:21:18,708
Of course. Thank goodness we had her on Lin Wan-li's case, right?

339
00:21:19,208 --> 00:21:22,000
Besides, she's my partner's crush.

340
00:21:22,083 --> 00:21:23,333
How could I not help?

341
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:27,958
I know you've got feelings for her.

342
00:21:29,333 --> 00:21:31,833
Hey, I know a specialist for this kind of thing.

343
00:21:31,916 --> 00:21:33,500
A love fixer.

344
00:21:35,916 --> 00:21:36,791
That's me.

345
00:21:36,875 --> 00:21:38,625
Let me teach you a few tricks, eh?

346
00:21:41,583 --> 00:21:44,791
Will we violate Ching He's rules if we take a side job?

347
00:21:45,291 --> 00:21:47,041
Fixer Celestial did assign this case.

348
00:21:48,750 --> 00:21:50,333
GERALD CHEN

349
00:21:51,250 --> 00:21:52,541
You're looking for him too?

350
00:21:53,041 --> 00:21:55,333
Someone asked me to find Gerald.

351
00:21:55,833 --> 00:21:56,875
Who is the client?

352
00:21:57,458 --> 00:21:59,375
I can't tell you.

353
00:21:59,458 --> 00:22:00,916
But finding Gerald

354
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:04,541
is very important to Ching He

355
00:22:04,625 --> 00:22:07,125
because this concerns our survival.

356
00:22:07,708 --> 00:22:12,750
Besides, Gerald has something important that belongs to Ching He.

357
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:17,750
A fixer from Yeh Yueh Tong is crucial to the survival of Ching He?

358
00:22:17,833 --> 00:22:19,250
Seriously?

359
00:22:19,875 --> 00:22:21,416
The chairman didn't say much.

360
00:22:22,458 --> 00:22:25,666
Are you going to tell Mina that Ching He is looking for Gerald too?

361
00:22:25,750 --> 00:22:27,625
No, we can't tell outsiders.

362
00:22:28,875 --> 00:22:32,583
Okay. Since it's assigned, there shouldn't be any big problem.

363
00:22:34,291 --> 00:22:36,083
But before we begin,

364
00:22:37,125 --> 00:22:39,500
I need a small favor from you.

365
00:22:39,583 --> 00:22:40,625
I don't lend money.

366
00:22:41,208 --> 00:22:42,208
Not lending money.

367
00:22:42,958 --> 00:22:46,041
…a rare appearance by former Interior Minister Jerome Hsueh

368
00:22:46,125 --> 00:22:47,375
and his two sons.

369
00:22:47,458 --> 00:22:50,541
Besides his eldest son, Tristan Hsueh, who is running for mayor,

370
00:22:50,625 --> 00:22:52,208
his younger son…

371
00:22:52,291 --> 00:22:54,291
He's your boss?

372
00:22:54,791 --> 00:22:56,875
Don't freak out. What is so surprising?

373
00:22:56,958 --> 00:23:00,208
My boss likes to be called Goldie, right?

374
00:23:00,708 --> 00:23:02,583
Hello, Mr. Goldie.

375
00:23:03,083 --> 00:23:04,333
You're being too polite.

376
00:23:04,416 --> 00:23:06,916
With Fee around, I feel safe.

377
00:23:07,625 --> 00:23:09,708
We'll chat more later. I'm hungry. Let's eat.

378
00:23:10,291 --> 00:23:11,875
Let's eat first. Come.

379
00:23:11,958 --> 00:23:12,791
Come on.

380
00:23:13,291 --> 00:23:15,291
Why didn't you say your boss is a big shot?

381
00:23:15,375 --> 00:23:16,375
So what?

382
00:23:16,458 --> 00:23:18,208
I didn't prepare much today.

383
00:23:18,291 --> 00:23:20,750
It's fine. Goldie prefers simple meals.

384
00:23:20,833 --> 00:23:23,208
It's just some simple lobster and fish.

385
00:23:23,291 --> 00:23:24,500
Dig in.

386
00:23:25,666 --> 00:23:26,875
Have some.

387
00:23:27,625 --> 00:23:31,833
Mr. Goldie, thank you for believing in Felix.

388
00:23:31,916 --> 00:23:36,375
You know, he is reentering the workforce during a midlife crisis.

389
00:23:36,458 --> 00:23:37,791
Finding a job isn't easy.

390
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:39,125
What midlife crisis?

391
00:23:39,208 --> 00:23:42,458
This is called getting back in the game.

392
00:23:43,083 --> 00:23:44,416
You're one to talk.

393
00:23:44,500 --> 00:23:47,125
Why didn't you tell me you sold off the gambling house?

394
00:23:47,208 --> 00:23:48,708
Now you know, don't you?

395
00:23:48,791 --> 00:23:50,208
Don't say that.

396
00:23:50,291 --> 00:23:52,875
I'm so lucky to have a bodyguard like Fee,

397
00:23:52,958 --> 00:23:56,958
who is having a midlife crisis and reentering the workforce.

398
00:23:57,041 --> 00:23:57,875
You're too kind.

399
00:23:58,625 --> 00:24:01,291
But why does Goldie need my dad's protection?

400
00:24:06,041 --> 00:24:08,208
Don't let his refined appearance fool you.

401
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:13,458
These ultra-rich heirs have a habit of picking fights and making enemies.

402
00:24:13,541 --> 00:24:16,458
That is when they need smart and capable people like us

403
00:24:16,541 --> 00:24:18,125
to help smooth things out.

404
00:24:18,208 --> 00:24:19,166
Got it?

405
00:24:19,250 --> 00:24:20,958
Yes. That's right.

406
00:24:21,041 --> 00:24:23,541
Oh gosh, what fell?

407
00:24:26,416 --> 00:24:29,000
To rich heirs who go around making enemies.

408
00:24:29,958 --> 00:24:32,000
How did the pot lid fall on its own?

409
00:24:32,083 --> 00:24:33,000
How should I know?

410
00:24:33,083 --> 00:24:35,208
-I didn't put it here. -She's nagging again.

411
00:24:35,291 --> 00:24:36,708
-Did it grow legs? -Eat up.

412
00:24:36,791 --> 00:24:39,041
I only carried the dishes. It was Dad.

413
00:24:39,125 --> 00:24:40,000
What's going on?

414
00:24:40,083 --> 00:24:42,875
Felix Chiang, the pot lid doesn't go here.

415
00:24:42,958 --> 00:24:44,375
You told me to put it here.

416
00:24:44,458 --> 00:24:45,708
No, I didn't.

417
00:24:45,791 --> 00:24:48,458
Don't be so loud. My boss is here.

418
00:24:48,541 --> 00:24:51,041
-Right. -Keep it together.

419
00:24:51,125 --> 00:24:53,833
I've been holding myself back a lot today.

420
00:24:53,916 --> 00:24:56,333
AUTHENTIC TIEN-BU-LA

421
00:24:59,666 --> 00:25:01,375
Okay, here comes the tien-bu-la.

422
00:25:02,666 --> 00:25:04,083
Yours without cilantro.

423
00:25:04,166 --> 00:25:05,000
Thank you.

424
00:25:05,083 --> 00:25:06,500
Hold on.

425
00:25:06,583 --> 00:25:09,416
You said both Zoe and William are in charge of Yuan Tao.

426
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:10,333
ARCADE

427
00:25:10,416 --> 00:25:11,708
Through William, we can…

428
00:25:11,791 --> 00:25:14,708
Find out how Zoe's death is connected to Gerald.

429
00:25:14,791 --> 00:25:16,333
That's easy.

430
00:25:16,416 --> 00:25:19,375
Kidnap William and just fucking beat him until he talks.

431
00:25:19,458 --> 00:25:22,125
That tactic might work on trash like Sheng.

432
00:25:22,208 --> 00:25:24,166
But for someone of his status,

433
00:25:24,666 --> 00:25:26,375
you don't know who is backing him.

434
00:25:26,458 --> 00:25:28,291
We have to be careful not to alert him.

435
00:25:29,375 --> 00:25:30,500
So tell me.

436
00:25:30,583 --> 00:25:32,125
How will you make him talk?

437
00:25:32,208 --> 00:25:35,333
To get people like him to talk, you need leverage that can ruin him.

438
00:25:35,416 --> 00:25:37,250
Use that leverage to make him comply.

439
00:25:37,750 --> 00:25:40,000
What leverage could you have against a crypto guy?

440
00:25:40,083 --> 00:25:42,208
We found evidence of him committing fraud.

441
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:45,708
My wife fell for a bogus coin like this.

442
00:25:47,041 --> 00:25:48,833
How did you get this information?

443
00:25:48,916 --> 00:25:51,000
Of course we did some legwork.

444
00:25:51,083 --> 00:25:53,083
-Should we have waited for you? -Did I ask you?

445
00:25:53,166 --> 00:25:55,333
Just swing your club. Don't butt in.

446
00:25:55,416 --> 00:25:57,541
What kind of legwork did you guys do?

447
00:26:04,958 --> 00:26:07,375
Damn, it's so windy. How am I supposed to play?

448
00:26:09,375 --> 00:26:10,208
Hello?

449
00:26:11,291 --> 00:26:12,416
Louis Hsueh?

450
00:26:14,333 --> 00:26:16,500
Sure, no problem.

451
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:18,708
Hey, is his brother coming?

452
00:26:20,625 --> 00:26:21,875
Okay, bye.

453
00:26:31,041 --> 00:26:32,416
Do you come here often?

454
00:26:32,916 --> 00:26:35,375
I do. My office is just next door.

455
00:26:35,458 --> 00:26:36,916
You mean Yuan Tao?

456
00:26:37,875 --> 00:26:38,708
You remember?

457
00:26:39,208 --> 00:26:40,958
It's in the first line of your bio.

458
00:26:41,458 --> 00:26:42,833
Right.

459
00:26:44,291 --> 00:26:45,125
Hey, tell me.

460
00:26:45,625 --> 00:26:47,916
Why do you use a dating app?

461
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:50,625
I mean, you don't look like you need it.

462
00:27:00,750 --> 00:27:02,125
Buy me another drink.

463
00:27:02,625 --> 00:27:03,541
And I'll tell you.

464
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:08,000
Okay.

465
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:10,708
I… I'll go order.

466
00:27:11,666 --> 00:27:12,833
I…

467
00:27:14,666 --> 00:27:16,583
Hey, excuse me. Um…

468
00:27:21,125 --> 00:27:23,000
Let me see. Um…

469
00:27:37,125 --> 00:27:39,208
PLEASE SCAN YOUR FINGERPRINT

470
00:27:51,625 --> 00:27:54,083
The Hsueh's low-key younger son sought me out.

471
00:27:54,166 --> 00:27:55,041
I'm flattered.

472
00:27:55,541 --> 00:27:57,291
-Let's tee off. We'll chat. -Sure.

473
00:27:58,208 --> 00:27:59,208
What a coincidence.

474
00:27:59,291 --> 00:28:02,125
I just ran into Tristan at the Chamber. We talked about you.

475
00:28:02,625 --> 00:28:03,916
What did my brother say?

476
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:25,500
Plug in the flash drive. The hacking software will install itself.

477
00:28:25,583 --> 00:28:28,041
You can grab files remotely from another computer.

478
00:28:28,541 --> 00:28:29,500
Thanks.

479
00:28:30,083 --> 00:28:31,791
Wait, aren't you buying me a meal?

480
00:28:31,875 --> 00:28:32,875
Next time.

481
00:28:33,416 --> 00:28:34,541
Next time again.

482
00:28:34,625 --> 00:28:35,708
I'm just being used.

483
00:28:37,750 --> 00:28:39,583
So he felt like you used him?

484
00:28:39,666 --> 00:28:40,625
That's not fair.

485
00:28:40,708 --> 00:28:41,541
Right?

486
00:28:41,625 --> 00:28:44,416
And I didn't tell him to drive me every day.

487
00:28:44,916 --> 00:28:46,875
I split the bills with him too.

488
00:28:47,375 --> 00:28:49,208
Anyway, we kept fighting, so we're done.

489
00:28:49,791 --> 00:28:50,958
Of course.

490
00:28:51,791 --> 00:28:54,333
Sorry, I drank too much. I'm going to use the restroom.

491
00:28:54,416 --> 00:28:55,375
Oh, okay.

492
00:28:56,708 --> 00:28:57,875
Is this yours?

493
00:28:59,875 --> 00:29:00,750
Oh, yes.

494
00:29:00,833 --> 00:29:02,041
-Wait for me. -Okay.

495
00:29:06,666 --> 00:29:09,375
You made that engineer wait until closing?

496
00:29:09,458 --> 00:29:10,291
What else, then?

497
00:29:12,208 --> 00:29:14,625
There's no information on Gerald in there.

498
00:29:14,708 --> 00:29:16,958
Yuan Tao seems like a normal business.

499
00:29:17,041 --> 00:29:18,625
But interestingly,

500
00:29:18,708 --> 00:29:21,833
a year and a half ago, Yuan Tao transferred a large sum of money

501
00:29:21,916 --> 00:29:24,750
to set up a new company called Tolita.

502
00:29:24,833 --> 00:29:27,958
The person in charge is this financial influencer.

503
00:29:28,041 --> 00:29:30,000
Hello, I'm Dolly. I'm happy to share…

504
00:29:30,083 --> 00:29:31,833
San He used to do this too.

505
00:29:31,916 --> 00:29:35,041
Gang leaders would hire front men to evade police scrutiny.

506
00:29:35,125 --> 00:29:36,500
And I discovered

507
00:29:36,583 --> 00:29:39,125
that Tolita was involved in fraud disputes.

508
00:29:39,208 --> 00:29:42,708
Those affected were likely placated, so the news was suppressed.

509
00:29:43,208 --> 00:29:45,625
This… This company, Tolita,

510
00:29:45,708 --> 00:29:48,541
I don't think it's enough to ruin William.

511
00:29:48,625 --> 00:29:50,875
That's why we keep digging. Why else are you here?

512
00:29:50,958 --> 00:29:53,000
Stop asking and do something, will you?

513
00:29:53,083 --> 00:29:55,333
Can you be more polite in front of a lady?

514
00:29:57,041 --> 00:29:58,458
That's where Dolly Bit helps.

515
00:29:58,541 --> 00:30:00,375
This is a brand-new opportunity

516
00:30:00,458 --> 00:30:03,458
to buy a high-potential crypto coin at an extremely low price.

517
00:30:05,625 --> 00:30:07,541
How come you want to invest in crypto?

518
00:30:07,625 --> 00:30:11,083
With your family's resources, you can start an investment firm.

519
00:30:11,166 --> 00:30:12,541
My brother likes politics.

520
00:30:12,625 --> 00:30:13,916
I prefer making money.

521
00:30:14,416 --> 00:30:15,625
Who would pass up money?

522
00:30:17,916 --> 00:30:19,125
So we share an interest.

523
00:30:19,208 --> 00:30:21,833
But I prefer it when everyone makes money.

524
00:30:22,666 --> 00:30:25,625
Lately, I've been watching a crypto coin.

525
00:30:25,708 --> 00:30:29,083
It's getting a lot of hype. It's called, um, Dolly Bit.

526
00:30:29,666 --> 00:30:31,833
It's recommended by a YouTuber called Dolly.

527
00:30:31,916 --> 00:30:33,000
Have you heard of it?

528
00:30:33,583 --> 00:30:34,541
I have.

529
00:30:34,625 --> 00:30:37,958
But that sort of obscure thing isn't right for you.

530
00:30:38,458 --> 00:30:39,916
You're so against it.

531
00:30:40,500 --> 00:30:41,750
You have some inside info?

532
00:30:44,041 --> 00:30:45,666
Only inside info on Yuan Tao

533
00:30:46,250 --> 00:30:49,208
that enables over 90% of my business partners to profit

534
00:30:49,291 --> 00:30:50,625
through range trading.

535
00:30:52,375 --> 00:30:53,208
Fuck.

536
00:30:53,916 --> 00:30:56,000
The wind sure is strange today.

537
00:30:57,666 --> 00:31:01,375
Members involved in the donation scandal will be thoroughly investigated,

538
00:31:01,458 --> 00:31:04,291
no matter who they are or which party they belong to.

539
00:31:04,375 --> 00:31:07,958
Sir, do you think someone is trying to manipulate public opinion?

540
00:31:09,666 --> 00:31:14,041
I've initiated disciplinary action to expel him from the party tomorrow.

541
00:31:14,541 --> 00:31:16,750
He's a legislator who has been supporting us.

542
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:17,750
If he finds out--

543
00:31:17,833 --> 00:31:19,541
He won't find out.

544
00:31:21,208 --> 00:31:24,125
To rise to the top, one has to be ruthless.

545
00:31:24,208 --> 00:31:26,666
If I must be sacrificed one day,

546
00:31:26,750 --> 00:31:28,083
then so be it.

547
00:31:32,666 --> 00:31:33,750
Also,

548
00:31:33,833 --> 00:31:35,500
I received a call.

549
00:31:35,583 --> 00:31:38,708
William from Yuan Tao said your brother reached out to him.

550
00:31:38,791 --> 00:31:40,666
He wants to invest in cryptocurrency.

551
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:43,125
What a small world.

552
00:31:43,208 --> 00:31:44,875
Dad, what do you want me to do?

553
00:31:46,500 --> 00:31:49,583
You both belong to the Hsueh family by blood.

554
00:31:50,083 --> 00:31:52,333
But he must be useful to you too.

555
00:31:52,833 --> 00:31:54,833
He will be helpful to us.

556
00:31:54,916 --> 00:31:57,666
Dad, you can trust my judgment.

557
00:31:59,541 --> 00:32:00,416
By the way,

558
00:32:00,500 --> 00:32:03,416
what did the doctor say at the follow-up visit?

559
00:32:03,500 --> 00:32:05,416
Let's focus on the fundraiser this week.

560
00:32:05,916 --> 00:32:07,291
We'll talk about that next week.

561
00:32:07,791 --> 00:32:09,500
Your work is our top priority.

562
00:32:16,583 --> 00:32:19,541
TRISTAN HSUEH

563
00:32:33,375 --> 00:32:34,500
What are you doing?

564
00:32:35,666 --> 00:32:36,666
Nothing.

565
00:32:36,750 --> 00:32:39,791
I'm testing how long I can hold a gun before my hand starts to shake.

566
00:32:39,875 --> 00:32:42,000
Who doesn't shake when they hold their hand up?

567
00:32:43,333 --> 00:32:44,458
That's true.

568
00:32:44,541 --> 00:32:47,333
With Parkinson's, don't your hands shake when they're at rest?

569
00:32:47,416 --> 00:32:49,541
The doctor said my case is special.

570
00:32:50,041 --> 00:32:53,541
The most annoying part is that I don't know when it will start to worsen.

571
00:32:54,166 --> 00:32:56,041
Using a gun is the last resort.

572
00:32:56,125 --> 00:32:58,000
Whether you can hold one matters little.

573
00:32:58,083 --> 00:33:01,333
What if my legs start getting stiff too?

574
00:33:05,041 --> 00:33:08,625
I saw that your brother's political crisis was all over the news.

575
00:33:08,708 --> 00:33:10,916
I don't need to worry about things in the family.

576
00:33:12,333 --> 00:33:15,916
As fixers, we always solve problems for others.

577
00:33:16,416 --> 00:33:19,416
But our own family problems are the hardest to fix.

578
00:33:20,500 --> 00:33:23,083
We gotta approach this investment adviser, Hung Kuo-lung.

579
00:33:23,583 --> 00:33:25,125
How is he related to Yuan Tao?

580
00:33:25,208 --> 00:33:27,708
He isn't. He just runs stock scams.

581
00:33:27,791 --> 00:33:31,500
We need you to play an easy mark to get concrete proof of William's fraud.

582
00:33:35,208 --> 00:33:36,666
Can you play mah-jongg?

583
00:33:37,291 --> 00:33:39,375
I'm super good at it.

584
00:33:43,375 --> 00:33:44,208
What?

585
00:33:44,291 --> 00:33:47,125
The membership is a non-refundable one-year contract.

586
00:33:47,208 --> 00:33:50,166
I'll recommend another one tomorrow. That's all. Bye.

587
00:33:52,041 --> 00:33:53,916
Hey, buddy.

588
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:56,208
If you have any sure bets, share them.

589
00:33:56,875 --> 00:33:57,958
What do you do?

590
00:33:58,041 --> 00:33:59,916
I haven't seen you here before.

591
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:02,000
I sell seafood. A small business.

592
00:34:02,916 --> 00:34:05,791
So are you investing your profits to stay ahead of inflation?

593
00:34:05,875 --> 00:34:07,250
Only cash makes me feel safe.

594
00:34:07,333 --> 00:34:08,291
That's not okay.

595
00:34:08,375 --> 00:34:10,166
Hey, young man, don't be like him.

596
00:34:10,250 --> 00:34:13,541
With inflation, your money will lose half its value in ten years.

597
00:34:13,625 --> 00:34:14,625
Who can you blame?

598
00:34:14,708 --> 00:34:16,791
Folks, can we begin?

599
00:34:17,291 --> 00:34:19,125
Right. I'm going first.

600
00:34:19,208 --> 00:34:20,375
Here, Red Dragon.

601
00:34:20,458 --> 00:34:23,083
My friend lost millions to an investment scam.

602
00:34:23,583 --> 00:34:25,791
Millions! Who would dare invest after that?

603
00:34:25,875 --> 00:34:27,916
-White Dragon. -White Dragon, kong.

604
00:34:29,541 --> 00:34:33,125
Let me ask you. Do you stop eating if you get diarrhea?

605
00:34:33,208 --> 00:34:36,958
You will eat food that doesn't give you diarrhea, right?

606
00:34:37,041 --> 00:34:39,958
Whoever called you still thinks you scammed them, don't they?

607
00:34:41,708 --> 00:34:45,791
Yes, lots of people get scammed out there.

608
00:34:46,416 --> 00:34:49,041
There are many scammers too.

609
00:34:51,083 --> 00:34:53,833
Just like the three of you.

610
00:34:55,125 --> 00:34:58,541
You guys have been exchanging glances from the beginning.

611
00:34:59,041 --> 00:35:00,500
If you want to hustle,

612
00:35:00,583 --> 00:35:02,625
get some more practice.

613
00:35:02,708 --> 00:35:03,541
Four Characters.

614
00:35:07,333 --> 00:35:09,125
I know how to play the game.

615
00:35:09,208 --> 00:35:11,375
Exposing you as hustlers

616
00:35:11,458 --> 00:35:12,916
won't end well for me.

617
00:35:13,541 --> 00:35:14,541
Here's what.

618
00:35:15,250 --> 00:35:17,458
Finish this round nicely,

619
00:35:17,541 --> 00:35:18,958
and let me win a little

620
00:35:19,041 --> 00:35:20,125
so everyone wins.

621
00:35:23,083 --> 00:35:24,500
We aren't hustlers.

622
00:35:24,583 --> 00:35:26,041
We know all about you.

623
00:35:26,708 --> 00:35:29,333
We need you, a hustler, to help us out.

624
00:35:29,875 --> 00:35:31,041
You want my help?

625
00:35:32,500 --> 00:35:33,625
Can you afford it?

626
00:35:51,500 --> 00:35:52,625
Hold on.

627
00:35:53,291 --> 00:35:54,416
Hold on.

628
00:35:55,791 --> 00:35:57,583
I'm getting old. I can't beat you.

629
00:35:57,666 --> 00:35:59,833
You couldn't beat me even when you were younger.

630
00:36:00,500 --> 00:36:02,291
Haven't you been busy lately?

631
00:36:02,375 --> 00:36:03,958
How come you're free for tennis?

632
00:36:04,958 --> 00:36:08,416
Ever since Tomb-Sweeping Day, Dad's health has noticeably worsened.

633
00:36:10,083 --> 00:36:11,583
I know you don't want to see him.

634
00:36:11,666 --> 00:36:13,125
It's not me.

635
00:36:13,708 --> 00:36:15,333
He doesn't want to see me.

636
00:36:17,125 --> 00:36:18,708
He heard that you're investing.

637
00:36:18,791 --> 00:36:20,166
He was quite happy.

638
00:36:22,208 --> 00:36:23,625
Did William say that?

639
00:36:24,791 --> 00:36:26,333
But my advice is,

640
00:36:26,416 --> 00:36:29,125
if you're going to invest, there are better options.

641
00:36:32,416 --> 00:36:33,833
What's wrong with William?

642
00:36:34,333 --> 00:36:35,541
How do you know him?

643
00:36:36,666 --> 00:36:39,541
There's nothing wrong with him. We just met at a cocktail party.

644
00:36:40,041 --> 00:36:43,375
I feel like he's not very honest or smart.

645
00:36:43,958 --> 00:36:45,583
Don't rush into investing with him.

646
00:36:51,708 --> 00:36:52,583
Come on.

647
00:36:53,125 --> 00:36:55,083
-You want to continue? -One last game.

648
00:36:55,583 --> 00:36:56,666
CANNON

649
00:36:58,625 --> 00:36:59,750
SOLDIER

650
00:36:59,833 --> 00:37:01,083
Check.

651
00:37:04,958 --> 00:37:07,041
That was a risky move.

652
00:37:07,541 --> 00:37:09,500
You only have a chariot and a cannon left,

653
00:37:10,416 --> 00:37:12,041
and you're rushing to give check?

654
00:37:17,583 --> 00:37:18,458
HORSE

655
00:37:19,958 --> 00:37:20,833
CHARIOT

656
00:37:21,458 --> 00:37:22,458
HORSE

657
00:37:22,541 --> 00:37:24,541
Who says I was going for the general?

658
00:37:27,583 --> 00:37:29,291
Once the surroundings are clear,

659
00:37:29,875 --> 00:37:32,125
will capturing the general be an issue?

660
00:37:32,791 --> 00:37:34,416
So are you here

661
00:37:34,916 --> 00:37:38,291
to protect or sacrifice the general?

662
00:37:44,250 --> 00:37:49,416
I can barely keep my elephant safe. How can I worry about anything else?

663
00:37:50,041 --> 00:37:51,916
Recently, there was a big case.

664
00:37:52,500 --> 00:37:54,583
My fixers screwed up.

665
00:37:54,666 --> 00:37:57,041
I was told that I'm too old

666
00:37:57,541 --> 00:37:59,625
and can't delegate properly.

667
00:37:59,708 --> 00:38:03,333
They said if I'm too old, I should step down.

668
00:38:03,875 --> 00:38:07,083
If they want you gone, they can find any excuse.

669
00:38:08,291 --> 00:38:10,416
I still need the old elephant that you are.

670
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:14,166
CHARIOT

671
00:38:14,250 --> 00:38:15,833
I'm just afraid that this elephant…

672
00:38:15,916 --> 00:38:17,333
ELEPHANT

673
00:38:17,416 --> 00:38:20,250
…will be taken out before it can protect you.

674
00:38:40,375 --> 00:38:41,333
Madam Fan.

675
00:38:50,250 --> 00:38:51,916
Keep an eye on Mina.

676
00:38:53,041 --> 00:38:54,833
See what she has found so far.

677
00:38:55,375 --> 00:38:56,208
Got it.

678
00:39:09,500 --> 00:39:12,166
Target Zoe confirmed dead.

679
00:43:05,625 --> 00:43:08,416
Subtitle translation by:
